From 76c3e18083e7ec8244bca7f31a3baa33d8129f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Studio shell: horizontal menubar replaces the sidebar; the
 workspace takes the width
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The brief: the vertical navigation took 216 px of every window and the top
bar's actions ran off the right edge at 1440; make it behave like a desktop
studio — tools horizontal at the top, revealed on demand, the canvas
dominant, nothing floating over the questionnaire.

Mapped first (docs/NAV-REDESIGN-MAP.md): every NAV entry by group, every
top-bar action, the mode cluster, and the 96 sidebar clicks, 17 active-tab
reads and 6 item listings across 52 browser suites.

- lib/menubar.ts (pure, tested): the four groups from the same NAV table
  the sidebar used, a one-line description per tool (the menu's preview),
  the Data Analytics link after Data, groupOfTab, fitGroups (fold from the
  right into More/Menu, reserving the More button), menuKey (WAI-ARIA
  menubar keys: ←/→ groups and switch an open menu, ↓ opens, ↑/↓ Home End
  inside, Enter, Esc returns focus).
- components/studio/MenuBar.tsx: Programming · Research Tools · Results ·
  Management │ Mode · 02 Grid, then "where am I" (group › tool · count ·
  environment) on the right. Hover-intent 140 ms or click opens; while one
  is open, moving across the bar switches at once; leaving closes after a
  220 ms grace; Escape and outside clicks close. Only the OPEN panel is in
  the DOM — twenty-five hidden tool names would shadow every
  `button:has-text("edit")` in the product. Group buttons carry
  data-nav-items / data-nav-keys so what a menu holds is knowable closed.
  Items: icon, name, count badge, description; the active tool and its
  group are marked. The Mode menu holds the five environments (radio, the
  Phase 5 test ids kept), Split with…, Focus and the chooser. Overflow
  measured with a hidden probe and a ResizeObserver; under 900 px the
  panel is a full-width sheet.
- Studio.tsx: the sidebar is gone; the menubar sits under the top bar;
  ModeSelector.tsx removed (its content is the Mode menu); the shell is a
  flex column (it was a 58px 1fr grid that put the first optional bar in
  the 1fr row); .ide-body is workspace + optional panel. Measured at 1440
  with Q1 selected: workspace 834 → 1050 px; the top bar fits.
- Focus in Studio mode (§8): the menubar tucks into a hairline you hover
  to reveal; unselected question cards go quiet. The Focus command applies
  in every mode now.
- Intelligent (§9): the example sentences are about the selected question.
- Chooser: the /sandbox page is exempt whatever ?dbid= it mounts — the
  suites mount mocked projects there, and Phase 5's chooser was standing
  in front of the insert bar in eleven of them.
- scripts/lib/nav.mjs: openTab / openTabKey / switchMode / modeMenuClick /
  navLabels / navCount — the two gestures a person makes. 52 suites
  rewritten mechanically; scripts/menubar-test.mjs (28 checks): shape,
  hover → see → click, keyboard end to end, never over the questionnaire,
  Mode menu + Focus, overflow at 600 px, ⌘K.
- Corpus: 98 of 105 pass; the 6 that fail are red on the pre-redesign tree
  too (recorded in docs/BROWSER-CORPUS.md); version-scoped-export needs
  Postgres and joins the exclusion list; .next-handoff ignored.

